  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:4952",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 appears to interact with BJ through multiple indirect pathways, all mediated by K-252a. The first pathway links Theasaponin E1 to the phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta, which is a target of K-252a. The second pathway connects Theasaponin E1 to solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is also a target of K-252a. The third pathway involves Theasaponin E1 targeting tyrosine-protein kinase Blk, which is a target of Gerontoisoflavone A, which in turn targets BJ. These pathways collectively suggest that Theasaponin E1 may influence BJ through a series of molecular interactions involving K-252a and its downstream targets. The integration of these evidence strands highlights a potential mechanism by which Theasaponin E1 could modulate BJ, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
